🗺️ The Full Roadmap
Phase 1 — Setup (Done / Almost Done)

✅ Install Python + PyCharm
✅ Install pandas, requests, matplotlib, plotly
✅ Get API key from football-data.org
✅ Run first API call and see raw data printing


Phase 2 — Data Fetching (Week 1)
Getting raw data from the API and understanding its structure
API → requests → raw JSON → print and explore

Fetch all World Cup matches
Fetch team info and group standings
Understand what fields exist (goals, dates, team names, status)
Save data to a CSV file so you don't have to call the API every time


Phase 3 — Data Cleaning (Week 1-2)
Turning messy raw JSON into usable tables
raw JSON → pandas DataFrame → clean table

Convert JSON to a DataFrame
Handle missing values (some scores are null before a match is played)
Filter by match status (FINISHED vs SCHEDULED)
Create new columns like total_goals, winner, points


Phase 4 — Analysis (Week 2-3)
Actually answering interesting questions with the data
Things you'll calculate:

Group standings (points, goal difference, goals scored)
Top scorers
Which teams score the most? Concede the most?
Average goals per match
Home vs away performance

All of this is just pandas — filtering, grouping, sorting

Phase 5 — Visualization (Week 3)
Turning your analysis into charts
pandas DataFrame → matplotlib/plotly → charts
Charts you'll make:

Bar chart of goals per team
Group standings table
Heatmap of match results
Line chart of goals over time as tournament progresses


Phase 6 — Prediction Model (Week 4)
The stats part — using a Poisson model to predict scores
What is Poisson? It's a simple statistical model that says:

"If Brazil scores 2.1 goals per game on average, what's the probability they score 0, 1, 2, 3... goals in their next match?"

team stats (pandas) → Poisson model (scipy) → score probabilities
Steps:

Calculate each team's average goals scored and conceded
Use scipy.stats.poisson to generate score probabilities
Predict most likely scoreline for upcoming matches
Compare predictions vs actual results


Phase 7 — Streamlit App (Week 5+)
Turning everything into a real interactive website
your Python code → Streamlit → web app anyone can use

Install Streamlit (pip install streamlit)
Build a simple dashboard with dropdowns and charts
Run it locally, then optionally deploy it free on streamlit.io
Share the link with friends



